WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.677 --> 00:00:06.753
- [Narrator] Salty, sweet, chewy, crunchy.

00:00:06.753 --> 00:00:08.631
It's a delicious combination born

00:00:08.631 --> 00:00:10.057
from one of Black America's most

00:00:10.057 --> 00:00:12.807
consequential cultural movements.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:20.917
It was the 1930s.

00:00:21.866 --> 00:00:23.453
The place was New York City.

00:00:23.453 --> 00:00:25.001
It was the epicenter of Black American's

00:00:25.001 --> 00:00:27.201
movement into mainstream culture.

00:00:27.201 --> 00:00:29.199
The Harlem Renaissance.

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:31.644
Artists, writers, and thinkers
would gather at venues

00:00:31.644 --> 00:00:33.925
in Harlem until the wee
hours of the morning.

00:00:33.925 --> 00:00:36.898
Listening to touring big
bands and jazz artists.

00:00:36.898 --> 00:00:38.734
As the clubs stayed open later and later,

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:40.079
so did the local restaurants to

00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:42.277
take in the hungry concert-goers.

00:00:42.277 --> 00:00:45.088
One such restaurant owner
was Joseph T. Wells,

00:00:45.088 --> 00:00:46.966
founder of Well's Supper Club.

00:00:46.966 --> 00:00:51.652
Well's became known for
its Southern-inspired menu.

00:00:51.652 --> 00:00:53.403
But Wells needed a hit to stay on top of

00:00:53.403 --> 00:00:55.845
the 2 a.m. restaurant business.

00:00:55.845 --> 00:00:57.262
What could he do?

00:00:58.539 --> 00:01:00.338
Seeing an opportunity, Wells realized that

00:01:00.338 --> 00:01:02.213
the fried chicken leftovers from dinner

00:01:02.213 --> 00:01:03.440
could be served with the freshly prepared

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:04.868
waffles for breakfast.

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:06.787
Creating a sweet and savory concoction

00:01:06.787 --> 00:01:08.537
unlike anything else.

00:01:10.939 --> 00:01:13.258
The dish was a hit.

00:01:13.258 --> 00:01:15.008
Eventually, word got out
and chicken and waffles

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:18.762
became a soul food staple
from Atlanta to Los Angeles.

00:01:18.762 --> 00:01:21.244
And though Well's closed in 1982,

00:01:21.244 --> 00:01:23.039
the dish lives on.

00:01:23.039 --> 00:01:25.156
So, when you think of
the Harlem Renaissance,

00:01:25.156 --> 00:01:28.905
take Duke Ellington's jazz,
Langston Hughes's poetry,

00:01:28.905 --> 00:01:32.322
and Joseph T. Wells' chicken and waffles.

